<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Gives Medieval Overhaul's cave snake faction a roster of reptile mamonos.

    Left alone, DankPyon_SnakeCave_Faction generates only MO's three giant snakes
    (lindwurm 10, giant constrictor 20, large cobra 40). This adds one reptile
    member kind to that Combat group and puts the species mix on the faction's
    xenotypeSet - the same pattern the rest of this mod uses, where a member's
    species comes from FactionDef.xenotypeSet and never from the pawnkind.

    Basilisks, medusas, lamias and wurms take 0.225 each. Omitting Baseliner from
    the list is deliberate: XenotypeSet.BaselinerChance is "one minus the sum of
    the non-baseliner chances", so a 0.9 roster leaves exactly 10% to Baseliner and
    a tenth of the members come out as ordinary humans. The four reptile faction
    rosters in Defs/FactionDefs/Factions_Reptile.xml use the same 0.9 convention.

    The member kind carries no xenotypeSet on purpose: a pawnkind-level set is a
    per-kind override and would shadow the faction roster (see the note in
    Defs/PawnKindDefs/PawnKinds_Reptile.xml).

    Guarding is done with PatchOperationConditional on the faction def, NOT with
    PatchOperationFindMod. That operation calls ModLister.HasActiveModWithName,
    which compares a mod's display name exactly rather than its package id, so a
    guard written against a package id never matches and turns the whole patch
    into a silent no-op with nothing in the log. Testing for the def itself is
    also the more honest test - it is the defName the patch actually needs.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="DankPyon_SnakeCave_Faction"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <success>Always</success>
      <operations>

        <!--
          The faction's humanlike member kind, added as a new def. Gear and stats
          mirror PMM_Reptile_BroodMember so a cave mamono is equipped like the other
          reptile faction members. It inherits PMM_ReptilePawnBase rather than
          PMM_BroodsBase so it does not inherit the Scalebound Broods default
          faction.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs</xpath>
          <value>
            <PawnKindDef ParentName="PMM_ReptilePawnBase">
              <defName>PMM_Reptile_CaveSnakeMember</defName>
              <label>cave dweller</label>
              <defaultFactionDef>DankPyon_SnakeCave_Faction</defaultFactionDef>
              <combatPower>55</combatPower>
              <itemQuality>Poor</itemQuality>
              <gearHealthRange>0.4~1.4</gearHealthRange>
              <apparelMoney>300~600</apparelMoney>
              <apparelTags>
                <li>Neolithic</li>
                <li>MedievalMilitary</li>
              </apparelTags>
              <apparelAllowHeadgearChance>0.5</apparelAllowHeadgearChance>
              <weaponMoney>120~250</weaponMoney>
              <weaponTags>
                <li>MedievalMeleeBasic</li>
              </weaponTags>
            </PawnKindDef>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          The species roster. 0.225 x 4 = 0.9, so the remaining tenth is
          Baseliner.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="DankPyon_SnakeCave_Faction"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <xenotypeSet>
              <xenotypeChances>
                <PMM_Reptile_Basilisk>0.225</PMM_Reptile_Basilisk>
                <PMM_Reptile_Medusa>0.225</PMM_Reptile_Medusa>
                <PMM_Reptile_Lamia>0.225</PMM_Reptile_Lamia>
                <PMM_Reptile_Wurm>0.225</PMM_Reptile_Wurm>
              </xenotypeChances>
            </xenotypeSet>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          Put the member kind into the Combat group next to MO's giant snakes. The
          weight is the knob for how much of the faction is mamonos rather than
          snakes: 70 against the snakes' 10+20+40 leaves the two halves even.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="DankPyon_SnakeCave_Faction"]/pawnGroupMakers/li[kindDef="Combat"]/options</xpath>
          <value>
            <PMM_Reptile_CaveSnakeMember>70</PMM_Reptile_CaveSnakeMember>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          The ruin's boss used to live here: a lamia "cave matriarch" placed on MO's
          DankPyon_BrigandLeader symbol. REMOVED 2026-09-24, do not re-add it.

          MO's ruin quests run QuestNode_GetSitePartDefsByTagsAndFaction before the node
          that sets enemyFaction, and that first node reads slate.Get("enemyFaction") as
          its preferred faction. It is null at that point, so SiteMakerHelper picks a
          random hostile faction for the site (siteFaction), vanilla's Util_GenerateSite
          builds the site with $siteFaction, and a KCSG symbol with spawnPartOfFaction
          true hands its pawn to the map's faction. So the whole garrison was another
          faction's pawns - insect mamonos in the report - and one lamia standing among
          them read as a mistake.

          Putting her back means making the ruin belong to the cave snakes, which takes
          reordering MO's quest nodes (offered, declined - user ruling 2026-09-24). Note
          also that the roster above only bites when a map really is owned by the cave
          snakes, and MO zeroes that faction's raid commonality.
        -->

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
